/target
**/*.rs.bk

# OpenMC HDF5 nuclear-data libraries are large (>100 MB); keep them out of git.
# The Doppler verification uses the extracted reference CSVs instead.
crates/njoy-outram-park-fork/tests/resources/*.h5

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/

# Session progress summaries (regenerated on demand; never committed)
/progress.md

# KOVAN proprietary literature is user-owned content that must never be
# committed (see crates/kovan-literature). The whole tree stays local.
crates/kovan-literature/proprietary/

# Artifacts *derived* from proprietary sources are equally user-owned, so the
# proprietary side of the generated tree stays local too. The open side
# (generated/bibtex/open/) is committed AND published — see the `exclude` list in
# crates/kovan-literature/Cargo.toml.
crates/kovan-literature/generated/bibtex/proprietary/
crates/kovan-literature/generated/markdown/proprietary/
crates/kovan-literature/generated/assets/proprietary/

# Generated outram-mc ↔ OpenMC-notebook comparison CSVs — reproducible from the
# verification tests + the .ipynb reference values; kept local, not committed.
crates/outram-mc-libs/verification_and_validation/openmc_notebook_comparisons/

# Raw source PDF of the Xin Wang (2018) UC Berkeley PhD dissertation
# (~9 MB, open literature: escholarship.org/uc/item/40q3985m). The committed
# deliverable is the extracted markdown in crates/nee_soon/docs/xin-wang-thesis/,
# not the binary. Keep the raw PDF local.
xin wang thesis.pdf
*thesis*.pdf

# ...but the kovan-literature OPEN archive is the exception: open-licensed source
# PDFs and their generated markdown ARE committed to GitHub, so collaborators get
# the literature with the repo. They are kept out of the *published crate* by the
# `exclude` list in crates/kovan-literature/Cargo.toml, not by gitignore — the
# two mechanisms serve different audiences (GitHub: yes, crates.io: no).
# proprietary/ stays ignored by its own rule above, and the negation is scoped to
# open/ so it can never re-admit a proprietary source. Generated markdown needs no
# negation — no rule ignores *.md in the first place.
!crates/kovan-literature/open/**/*.pdf

# Local staging area for literature being imported into kovan-literature. Raw
# source PDFs and their scratch conversions land here first; the committed
# deliverables are the generated markdown/BibTeX under
# crates/kovan-literature/generated/. Staging stays local so the same document
# is not committed twice (once as scratch, once as a generated artifact).
/kovan_import/

# Local staging area for collaborator (e.g. Ethan) work, to be merged into the
# proper crates later. Never committed — raw external WIP stays out of git until
# it has been reviewed for licensing / data-policy / GPLv3 compliance and
# integrated into the right crate.
/collaboration/

# Claude Code agent worktrees — transient isolated checkouts the harness creates
# for background subagents (isolation: "worktree"). Working scratch only, never
# committed; they are auto-cleaned when the agent finishes.
.claude/worktrees/

# Vendored upstream sources for reference/validation (e.g. NJOY2016 built to
# generate golden tapes for V&V). Large third-party trees — never committed
# (workspace vendor rule, bead op-264). GPLv3-compatible upstreams only.
/vendor/

# KOPITIAM per-project session memory (`.kopitiam/state.redb`), written when
# kopitiam runs in this repo. Local scratch state belonging to the tool, not to
# this project — never committed. The kopitiam source itself is a SEPARATE
# clone outside this tree (see the "Dogfood KOPITIAM" rule in CLAUDE.md); it
# must never be vendored or nested inside this workspace.
.kopitiam/

# Generated token-usage summary — the source of truth is the per-commit
# API-Usage trailers in the git log (query via docs/historian/token_usage.py).
# This markdown is a regenerable local summary, not tracked (was causing
# recurring merge conflicts as a generated file committed on many branches).
docs/token-usage.md
.aider*
